Aerie-Purpose: Let the settings page read and write the Widevine opt-in, which lives in Local State.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc (allowlist)
Aerie-Kind: hook

settingsPrivate finds a pref in the profile first and in Local State second
(PrefsUtil::FindServiceForPref), so one allowlist line is enough. The name is a string
literal, the same as aerie_widevine::kWidevineEnabled in components/aerie_widevine, to
keep the settings code free of a new dependency. A test in tests/ compares the two.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -476,4 +476,6 @@
   (*s_allowlist)[::prefs::kWebRTCIPHandlingPolicy] =
       settings_api::PrefType::kString;
+  // Aerie: the Widevine opt-in (Local State).
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.widevine.enabled"] = settings_api::PrefType::kBoolean;
 
   // Privacy page
